==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|carpentrie}}, from {{der|en|xno|carpenterie}}, from {{der|en|fro-nor|-}} (compare {{cog|fr|charpenterie}}). See [[carpenter]].

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|en}}
* {{hyphenation|en|carp|entry}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-carpentry.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q203605}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} The trade of cutting and joining [[timber]] in order to construct [[building]]s or other structures; [[woodworking]].
# {{senseid|en|workshop}} {{lb|en|countable}} A [[carpenter]]'s [[workshop]].
# {{senseid|en|timber}} {{lb|en|uncountable}} A [[collection]] of [[timber]] connected by being [[frame]]d together, as the pieces of a roof, floor, etc.; work done by a [[carpenter]].
#: {{ux|en|Fine '''carpentry''' for sale.}}

